# Mandatory Design System

**Scope:** All client UI layers (`lib/features/`, `lib/ui/`, and client components). UX behavior: **`interaction-ux.mdc`**. Structure: **`architecture-and-state.mdc`**.

---

## 1) Localization — Zero Hardcoded UI Strings

- Keep all locale dictionaries synchronized (e.g., `lib/l10n/app_en.arb` + `app_ar.arb`, or project i18n JSON/TS files) with full RTL and LTR support.
- Access strings only through the project's localization helper (e.g., `AppLocalizations.of(context)!` / `l10n` helper / `useTranslations()`).
- **NEVER** hardcode user-facing English or Arabic text inside widgets or components.
- Add localization keys **before** writing new UI copy.
- Dynamic user-generated content (names, message bodies, posts, server titles) is displayed as-is — never pass user content through UI translation lookups.

### Content Text Direction (Script-Aware, Not App Locale)

User-authored text must follow the **content's own script**, not the app chrome `Directionality`:

- Display: use shared content-bidi wrappers (e.g., `ContentDirectionality` / `ContentText` / `MentionTextWidget` in mobile, or `dir="auto"` in web).
- Layout: resolve alignment via script layout helpers (`contentTextLayoutFor` / `composerInputLayoutFor`) — `CrossAxisAlignment.start`, `AlignmentDirectional`, `TextAlign.start`.
- Composers: bind `textDirection` and `textAlign` dynamically to `composerInputLayoutFor(controller.text)` and preserve natural caret position via natural-edit caret helpers.
- **Forbidden:** `isArabic ? TextAlign.right : TextAlign.left` (or hardcoding alignment from app locale) for user content.

---

## 2) Colors — Semantic Theme / Context Tokens Only

| Layer | Role |
| --- | --- |
| Theme / palette files | Define raw hex values — theme/palette or CSS token sources only |
| **Semantic context/theme layer** | Theme-aware getters on `BuildContext` (`AppContextColors`) or CSS variables (`tokens.css`) — **only** layer UI consumes |
| Feature / widget / component code | Consumes semantic tokens (`context.*` / CSS vars) only |

- Use semantic getters (`context.textPrimary`, `context.textSecondary`, `context.brandPrimary`, `context.danger`, `context.materialWhite`, `context.surfaceCard`, `context.scaffoldBackground`, etc.).
- **Never** use raw hex values, static palette classes (`AppColors.*`), raw framework constants (`Colors.white`, `Colors.black`, `Colors.red`), or bare `Theme.of(context).cardColor` in feature or shared widget code.
- Scaffold / page canvas: use the semantic canvas token (`scaffoldBackground` / `webBackground`) — **never** pure black (`#000000` / `pureBlack`) except immersive fullscreen media (stories, fullscreen image/video viewers).
- Surface fills: use `context.surfaceCard` / semantic surface tokens — never ad-hoc card colors.
- Material mirrors: use `context.materialWhite`, `context.materialBlack`, `context.transparent` instead of `Colors.white` / `Colors.black` / `Colors.transparent`.
- Missing semantic color → add a getter on the semantic context/token layer; never hardcode in the widget.
- **Never** use `withOpacity()` — always `withValues(alpha: …)` on `context.*`.

### Padding & Insets

- Prefer **`EdgeInsets.symmetric`**, **`EdgeInsets.all`**, **`EdgeInsets.only`**, or **`EdgeInsetsDirectional`** — **never** **`EdgeInsets.fromLTRB`**.
- When axes differ, start from `EdgeInsets.symmetric(...)` and refine with **`.copyWith(...)`**.

---

## 3) Typography — Shared Scale Helpers Only

- Always use the project's shared typography scale helpers (e.g., `font*W*` from `text_style.dart` + settings/theme controller, or design-system typography tokens).
- **Never** construct raw `TextStyle(...)`, bare `Theme.textTheme` overrides, or unscaled text styles directly in features.
- Override only via `.copyWith(...)` on the shared helper, passing colors via `context.*`.

### Fixed Height on Text — Forbidden

- **Never** set `TextStyle(height: …)` or `.copyWith(height: …)` for layout control.
- **Never** wrap primary text in a fixed-`height` `SizedBox` or `Container` (clips scaled system fonts and longer translations).
- Constrain text safely using `maxLines` + `TextOverflow.ellipsis`, or `Flexible` / `Expanded`.

### Content Font Family (Script-Aware, Not App Locale)

- Messages & user content: use per-script font resolvers (`buildMessageFontStyle` / `buildScriptAwareFontStyle`) assigning appropriate Arabic and Latin font families dynamically.
- App chrome: use configured system font families (`systemArabicFontFamily` / `systemEnglishFontFamily`).
- Mixed scripts: set primary `fontFamily` plus `fontFamilyFallback` for the secondary script.
- **Forbidden:** tying user message fonts to app chrome locale alone.

```dart
Text(
  l10n.hello,
  style: font20W500(context, color: context.textPrimary),
)
```

---

## 4) Icons — Unified Icon System Only

- Use the project's designated icon library exclusively across features and shared UI (e.g., `HugeIcon` + `HugeIcons.*`, or the single icon pack defined in the design system).
- **Forbidden:** raw Material `Icons.*`, `Icon(Icons…)`, or `IconData` for display glyphs when the project standardizes on a unified icon pack.
- Shared buttons/tiles must accept the unified icon type rather than Material `IconData`.
- Apply color from `context.*` and size in logical pixels — **no** `.sp` or ScreenUtil scaling on new code.
- Inside circular or fixed-size boxes, wrap with `alignment: Alignment.center` or `Center` so glyphs never stretch.

```dart
HugeIcon(
  icon: HugeIcons.strokeRoundedHome01,
  color: context.textSecondary,
  size: 24,
)
```

---

## 5) Layout Sizing — No ScreenUtil on New or Touched Code

- **Do not** use `flutter_screenutil` (`.sp`, `.w`, `.h`, `.r`) on **new or touched** UI.
- Use logical pixels, `MediaQuery`, `LayoutBuilder`, `Flexible` / `Expanded`, and `SafeArea`.
- When editing legacy widgets that still use ScreenUtil, remove `.sp`/`.w`/`.h`/`.r` in the same change.
- Breakpoints: use responsive helpers (`ResponsiveHelper.isDesktop()`, `maxContentWidth`) for layout structure only — never for arbitrary font/padding scaling.
- Prefer width-driven fluid layouts; maintain touch targets **≥ 44×44** logical pixels.

---

## 6) App Bars & Toolbars

- Prefer shared **`UniversalAppBar`** / **`UniversalSliverAppBar`** over raw `AppBar`.
- Hero/cover screens: use shared **`FixedScreenToolbar`** + **`HeroToolbarBar`** so the back button stays pinned beneath the status bar — **never** place the sole back control inside a scrolling cover header.
- Title + actions: compose with `Row` / `Expanded` / `Flexible` / `FittedBox(fit: BoxFit.scaleDown)` matching shared toolbar helpers.
- Keep navigation intuitive: one obvious back control at the top of the viewport.

---

## 7) Tabs

- Default: **`TabController` + `TabBar` + `TabBarView`** — single controller supporting tap and swipe; never maintain duplicate index variables or replace `TabBarView` with `IndexedStack` unless swipe must be disabled (document why).
- Labels: set `labelColor`, `unselectedLabelColor`, and shared `font*W*` styles explicitly — do not set label colors transparent while hand-rolling custom child text colors.
- Pill indicator: `TabBar(indicator: BoxDecoration(…), indicatorSize: TabBarIndicatorSize.tab)`.
- Heavy tabs: use lazy tab wrappers (`LazyTabView`) inside `TabBarView`.
- Badges: use **`Badge`** + scoped **`BlocSelector`** (or fine-grained selector) bound to that tab only.

---

## 8) Text Inputs (Mandatory)

| Use Case | Primitive |
| --- | --- |
| Search, dialogs, inline fields, composers | Shared **`AppTextField`** (or project primary text field wrapper) |
| Labeled auth / settings forms | Shared **`DefaultFormField`** / **`DefaultPasswordFormField`** |
| Chat / comment composer chrome | Shared **`UniversalMessageInputField`** |

- **Never** instantiate raw `TextField` / `TextFormField` outside the shared text-field module.
- Default `autofocus: false` unless search or rename explicitly requires immediate keyboard focus.

---

## 9) Shared Widgets & Primitives — Use, Never Duplicate

Reuse and extend the project's shared widget/component suite rather than writing feature-local copies:

| Concern | Use Shared Primitive | Never in Features |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Network images & avatars | `AppCachedImage`, `AppAvatarImage` (or project cached wrapper) | Raw `CachedNetworkImage` / `Image.network` / bare `<img>` |
| Local image files | `AppLocalImageFile` | Raw `Image.file` |
| Image load errors | `AppImageErrorWidget` | Ad-hoc grey fallback containers |
| UI glyphs | Unified icon pack (`HugeIcon` + `HugeIcons.*`) | Raw `Icons.*` / mixed icon packs |
| App bar / hero toolbar | `UniversalAppBar`, `HeroToolbarBar` | Raw `AppBar` (unless documented) |
| List/feed loading | `Skeletonizer` + semantic skeleton tokens | Full-screen spinner for list bodies |
| Bottom sheets | `showAppModalBottomSheet` + `AppBottomSheetBody` | Raw modal sheet without bottom safe inset |
| Dialogs / confirm | `showAppDialog`, `showConfirmationDialog`, `AppButton` | Bare `AlertDialog` / unconfirmed destructive ops |
| Comments sheets | Shared `showCommentsSheet` | Duplicate sheet per screen |
| Fullscreen media | `DragToDismissMedia` (`panEnabled` only when zoomed) | Raw `InteractiveViewer` alone |
| Call video | `CallVideoRenderer` + mirror policy helper | Raw renderer / inline `Transform.flip` |
| Text input | Shared field family above | Raw `TextField` / `TextFormField` |
| Content bidi | `ContentDirectionality`, `contentTextLayoutFor` | Manual alignment via `isArabic` |
| Badged icons | `AppBadgedIconButton`, `AppBadgeOverlay` | Badge stealing touch events |
| Tap guard | `AppButton` / `guardTap` | Unguarded async multi-tap handlers |
| UI sounds | `uiSound` service | Ad-hoc `AudioPlayer` in features |

- **Images:** pass only `memCacheWidth` **or** `memCacheHeight` (never both) unless the container is strictly square. Use skeleton placeholders matching theme tokens.
- **Media overlays:** Overlays (play buttons, status chips, close icons) above constrained media (`ConstrainedBox(maxHeight: ...)`, `AspectRatio`) must use `Positioned.fill(child: IgnorePointer(...))` or bounded stack alignment. **Never** place an unconstrained `Center(...)` inside a constrained media wrapper, as it causes phantom vertical/horizontal letterboxing.
- **UI sounds:** play send sounds (e.g., `messageSent`) **only after** backend/server confirmation — never on optimistic insert. Play receive notifications on foreground push arrival.
- **Calls:** keep call video chrome in **LTR** (`Directionality`), applying mirror transforms strictly as display-only via the mirror policy helper.

---

## 10) Do Not

- Expand legacy/frozen web targets inside mobile codebases when a dedicated web app exists.
- Use ScreenUtil scaling (`.sp`, `.w`, `.h`, `.r`) on new or touched UI.
- Hardcode user-facing strings or raw framework icons in feature UI.
- Use pure black (`#000000`) as normal scaffold/page canvas background.
- Duplicate shared primitives — extend the shared component instead.
